From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:38:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-microsoft-denali: Add audio playback
 over DisplayPort

The Surface Pro 11 has two USB-C ports with DisplayPort alt mode, driven
by mdss_dp0 and mdss_dp1. Both controllers register an HDMI audio codec,
but the sound card links only the speakers and the microphones, so a
monitor or dock connected over USB-C gets no audio.

Link the two controllers to the DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0 and DISPLAY_PORT_RX_1
backends, as on the ThinkPad T14s and the CRD. The machine driver
already creates the DP0 and DP1 jacks for these links.

Tested with a monitor on the mdss_dp1 port playing through its speaker
jack.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi    | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
index 230f2da1a..b2e1fedc7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
@@ -359,6 +359,38 @@ sound {
 				"VA DMIC0", "vdd-micb",
 				"VA DMIC1", "vdd-micb";
 
+		displayport-0-dai-link {
+			link-name = "DisplayPort0 Playback";
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&mdss_dp0>;
+			};
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apm>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		displayport-1-dai-link {
+			link-name = "DisplayPort1 Playback";
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&mdss_dp1>;
+			};
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX_1>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6apm>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		wsa-dai-link {
 			link-name = "WSA Playback";
 
